senses
  entry
    definition "the seat within a bishop's diocese where the bishop's cathedral is located"
    id oewn-08604380-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "perceive by sight or have the power to perceive by sight"
    examples ("You have to be a good observer to see all the details" "Can you see the bird in that tree?" "He is blind — he cannot see")
    id oewn-02133754-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "perceive (an idea or situation) mentally"
    examples ("Now I see!" "I just can't see your point" "Does she realize how important this decision is?" "I don't understand the idea")
    id oewn-00592510-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (understand realize realise)
  entry
    definition "perceive or be contemporaneous with"
    examples ("We found Republicans winning the offices" "You'll see a lot of cheating in this school" "The 1960's saw the rebellion of the younger generation against established traditions" "I want to see results")
    id oewn-02133338-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (witness find)
  entry
    definition "imagine; conceive of; see in one's mind"
    examples ("I can't see him on horseback!" "I can see what will happen" "I can see a risk in this strategy")
    id oewn-01638974-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (visualize visualise envision project fancy figure picture image)
  entry
    definition "deem to be"
    examples ("She views this quite differently from me" "I consider her to be shallow" "I don't see the situation quite as negatively as you do")
    id oewn-00692380-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (consider reckon view regard)
  entry
    definition "get to know or become aware of, usually accidentally"
    examples ("I learned that she has two grown-up children" "I see that you have been promoted")
    id oewn-00600349-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (learn hear "get word" "get wind" "pick up" "find out" "get a line" discover)
  entry
    definition "see or watch"
    examples ("view a show on television" "This program will be seen all over the world" "view an exhibition" "Catch a show on Broadway" "see a movie")
    id oewn-02155378-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (watch view catch "take in")
  entry
    definition "come together"
    examples ("I'll probably see you at the meeting" "How nice to see you again!")
    id oewn-02026953-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (meet "run into" encounter "run across" "come across")
  entry
    definition "find out, learn, or determine with certainty, usually by making an inquiry or other effort"
    examples ("I want to see whether she speaks French" "See whether it works" "find out if he speaks Russian" "Check whether the train leaves on time")
    id oewn-00922307-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (determine check "find out" ascertain watch learn)
  entry
    definition "be careful or certain to do something; make certain of something"
    examples ("He verified that the valves were closed" "See that the curtains are closed" "control the quality of the product")
    id oewn-00664507-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (check insure "see to it" ensure control ascertain assure)
  entry
    definition "go to see for professional or business reasons"
    examples ("You should see a lawyer" "We had to see a psychiatrist")
    id oewn-02493953-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "go to see for a social visit"
    examples ("I went to see my friend Mary the other day")
    id oewn-02494137-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "go to see a place, as for entertainment"
    examples ("We went to see the Eiffel Tower in the morning")
    id oewn-02498679-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (visit)
  entry
    definition "take charge of or deal with"
    examples ("Could you see about lunch?" "I must attend to this matter" "She took care of this business")
    id oewn-02555278-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (attend "take care" look)
  entry
    definition "receive as a specified guest"
    examples ("the doctor will see you now" "The minister doesn't see anybody before noon")
    id oewn-01473299-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "date regularly; have a steady relationship with"
    examples ("Did you know that she is seeing an older man?" "He is dating his former wife again!")
